WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.080
- [Narrator] Chipotle's
menu only has a few items,

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.880
but it's highly customizable.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.790
Born in 1993, that's what's made Chipotle

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.950
one of the most successful fast casual

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.840
restaurant chains in the U.S.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.440
But in recent years, Chipotle's
faced many challenges.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.810
Between 2015 to 2018,

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.320
Chipotle dealt with five
foodborne illness outbreaks.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.150
Like most of the restaurant industry,

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.100
Chipotle's revenue took a big hit

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.650
during the beginning of
the Coronavirus pandemic.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.780
And today it's dealing with inflation

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.410
that's increased labor,
transportation, and food costs.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.940
Yet despite these setbacks,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.430
Chipotle's sales are actually growing.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.060
Here's how Chipotle's focus
on efficiency and innovation

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.610
helped it bounce back and
become one of the country's

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.250
most valuable quick service chains.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.737
This is "The Economics of Chipotle."

00:00:51.236 --> 00:00:54.660
Chipotle's revenue has
increased by more than 200%

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.070
over the past decade.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:59.160
Its stock price has increased about 400%

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.230
in the last five years.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.900
Much of Chipotle's success
comes from its efficient

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.690
and what it calls "transparent"
in-store experience.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.030
- Chipotle has really, in a lot of ways,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.720
made the whole fast casual
category for restaurants.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.330
It's not fast food, it's not full service.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.370
They've generated a lot of sales

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.260
from people who want this alternative

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.920
that's seems fresher and
faster than fast food,

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.080
but is not a full service experience.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.780
Fast casual design can help them reduce

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.170
some of their labor expenses,
which helps with profits.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.910
- [Narrator] Chipotle's
menu is relatively small

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.380
but it's easy to customize.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.050
- There's tons of stuff
you can put on your meal.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:40.710
That's proteins, that's
cheeses, that's vegetables,

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.690
that's all the salsas and sauces.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:45.960
And for a customer that makes it exciting.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.490
You know, they get lots
of different things

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.140
they can customize their meal with.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.150
The more limited menu in general

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.370
is better for restaurants
and their profits.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.400
It's less things to train
the restaurant workers on.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.780
It's less waste.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.700
- [Narrator] Chipotle's founder Steve Ells

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.860
emphasized having an open kitchen.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.290
He wanted customers to be
able to see the ingredients

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.420
and preparation in front of them.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.000
Today, employees work
at individual stations

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.980
to serve already-prepared ingredients,

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.220
making the ordering process
more efficient for customers.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.560
- We can serve as many as 100 customers

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.970
within a 15-minute period.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.340
What's a better way than
telling people that it's fresh?

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.173
Showing them.

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:22.680
Let them come in and
discover for themselves.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.960
- [Narrator] This transparency
has been very important

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:28.620
for Chipotle, especially
after its food safety issues.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.470
After several outbreaks
of E. coli, Salmonella,

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.750
and Norovirus in Chipotle restaurants,

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.120
the company implemented several changes

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.090
like improving food preparation
and storage procedures,

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.550
encouraging sick
employees to stay at home,

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.400
and bringing on a new CEO, Brian Niccol.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.110
- He really did emphasize

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.450
that they cleaned up their procedures.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:49.710
Didn't happen immediately.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.170
But with time, people
start to forget things too.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:55.500
There hasn't been the
big high-profile scares

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.060
that there were previously.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.600
- [Narrator] After several
outbreaks between 2015 and 2018,

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.430
Chipotle's stock price took a hit.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.550
However, its focus on its
digital ordering platforms

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:09.810
helped drive up revenue and
stock prices started to climb.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.720
Back in 2008, Chipotle
became one of the first

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.260
fast casual chains to create
an online store pickup model.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.780
In its first year,
Chipotle's digital sales

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:23.310
accounted for $13 million, or
just 1% of its total sales.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:27.750
In 2022, digital sales
grew to $3.4 billion.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.120
That's now nearly 40% of Chipotle's

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.590
food and beverage revenue.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.720
- If you're ordering online digitally,

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.610
that is made for you

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.380
at a whole separate part of the kitchen,

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.830
which is just dedicated to online orders.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.020
- [Narrator] Chipotle's app
and online ordering systems

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.150
were also vital during the pandemic.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.820
- The pandemic obviously was
terrible for all restaurants.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.310
But Chipotle did have
some advantages there

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:53.610
in that they had this whole
digital ordering platform

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:56.670
really set up and scaled beforehand.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.140
- When the pandemic first hit,

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.910
we saw that people stopped
going to restaurants

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:00.743
for some period of time.

00:04:00.743 --> 00:04:03.780
So we saw our sales drop
pretty significantly.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:05.640
But it only took, like, a week or two

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.530
before we started to see that

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.930
while they first stopped
visiting restaurants,

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:12.360
the adoption of the digital ordering

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:13.890
really picked up very, very quickly.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.260
And so I would say within
the first four weeks,

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:20.670
we had our digital ordering
soar from about 18%

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.710
to it at one point hit 70%.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:24.510
- [Narrator] Chipotle
also designed its stores

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:27.570
to have two separate prep
stations called make lines.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.240
One make line is just for in-store orders,

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.420
and the other is for
digital and catering orders.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.980
This made food pickups quicker

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.740
for customers who didn't
want to spend time indoors.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.470
- This idea that we had
the digital make line

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.030
so that as people were ordering,

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.770
we could make food on
their digital make line,

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:46.590
and also serve customers that
were choosing to come in.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.120
So it was a seamless experience.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.520
Like most stocks during 2020,

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.220
they were still lower than
they were before the pandemic.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.710
But by the end of the first
year into the second year,

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.080
most stocks had, you
know, fully recovered.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.120
We had our all time high in 2021.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.670
- [Narrator] Recently, Chipotle
has continued to expand

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:04.200
its digital ordering services

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.680
with a new pickup option for
customers called Chipotlanes.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.070
- Let's go ahead and
offer all the convenience

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:13.950
of the drive-through, but
when you order ahead of time,

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.530
you know exactly what time to
come, and so there's no line.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.720
You drive up and you pull to our window,

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.220
you get your food, and off you go.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.830
- [Narrator] The first
Chipotlane opened in 2018,

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:26.220
and there are already
nearly 600 across the U.S.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:29.340
Chipotle says at least 80%
of new restaurant locations

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:32.160
opening in 2023 will have Chipotlanes.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.290
But that's just one
example of how Chipotle

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:37.110
has continued to innovate
to attract customers.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.420
- Social media has been
great for us because

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.910
in addition to making sure we're serving,

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.650
you know, the meals that customers come

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.090
to expect at Chipotle,

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:46.890
we also want to be part of a culture.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:48.840
- [Narrator] Chipotle
frequently uses social media

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:52.410
to attract younger consumers
by releasing recipe videos,

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.560
animated short films, Roblox games,

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:56.970
and social media campaigns

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:59.880
like the lid flip challenge
with major influencers.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:03.360
Chipotle has also used social
media to drum up excitement

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.450
about new menu items and
innovate its menu options

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.250
to keep up with consumer trends.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.930
- Adding new things for customers

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.430
is very important to Chipotle,

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.080
and they have a whole process for this

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:17.310
where they try and try
these items in-house

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.520
and really test and learn
before they test in stores.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.880
They like Menu News,
whether it's, you know,

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:28.230
a steak item or a chicken
item, Al Pastor, quesadillas.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.720
They want to keep customers interested,

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.540
even if most of their
menu is staying the same.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.820
- [Narrator] So what's next for Chipotle?

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:38.010
- In general, the online ordering,

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.690
even when you pick it
up in the restaurant,

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:41.430
is just much more efficient.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:42.990
- [Narrator] The company
says it wants to open

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:46.710
more locations that are only
used for online pickup orders.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.140
They won't have any seating for customers.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.540
This will also cut down on labor costs,

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.820
since workers won't need
to clean seating areas

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.260
and bathrooms as often.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:57.210
- We think the idea is
let the customers choose

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.500
which channel they want.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:01.350
Now our job is to make sure
every channel is convenient,

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.970
it's easy, it's fast,

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.950
so that we don't give
any friction whatsoever.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:07.470
But make sure every experience
that you can provide

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:09.344
in every channel is a great one.

00:07:09.344 --> 00:07:11.927
(gentle music)

